---
// Generated API inventory: routes from the daemon's own server.go.
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import docs from '../../generated/docs.json';
---
<Docs title="API reference · KeepState docs" description="The ksd daemon's HTTP surface, synced from its route table.">
  <h1>API reference</h1>
  <p>
    The daemon listens on <code>127.0.0.1:7440</code> inside the bench
    host. The CLI is a thin client over these {docs.routes.length} routes;
    anything the CLI does, the API does. Full request and response schemas
    arrive with the han protocol documentation.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {docs.routes.map((r) => (
        <tr><td><code>{r.method}</code></td><td><code>{r.path}</code></td></tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Sessions are created with <code>POST /sessions</code>, frozen with
    <code>POST /sessions/&lbrace;id&rbrace;/checkpoint</code>, woken with
    <code>POST /sessions/&lbrace;id&rbrace;/resume</code>, branched with
    <code>POST /sessions/&lbrace;id&rbrace;/fork</code>. <code>POST /gc</code>
    plans by default and deletes only with <code>?apply=1</code>.
  </p>
</Docs>
